cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "slippage-predictor"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Natale"
    given-names: "Francesco"
repository-code: "https://github.com/francescopionatale/slippage-predictor"
abstract: >-
  A research-grade framework for estimating order execution cost
  (slippage) from public intraday OHLCV data. It pairs a methodologically
  careful synthetic square-root-impact proxy with an empirical,
  non-circular real-data target (forward Amihud illiquidity / Kyle's
  lambda), gradient-boosting baselines, a distributional quantile head,
  and Diebold-Mariano significance testing.
keywords:
  - market-microstructure
  - transaction-cost-analysis
  - slippage
  - quantitative-finance
  - pytorch
  - walk-forward
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
